19378	{"artifactId":"LLD-9a7bbe63297457c2-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-9a7bbe63297457c2-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-06T16:41:47.967Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of the seven user decisions cited as c9 is designed, and the one thing dropped (milestones) is not built.","evidence":"There is no upstream DEF/SPEC to compare against: Glob .insrc/artifacts/*9a7bbe63* returns only LLD-9a7bbe63297457c2-s1.json, so the intent is the c9 list in the design itself (a chat statement I cannot read back from the repo). Against that list: epic item on Define approval (3.2 DEFINE), story on LLD approval (3.2 EPIC STORY DESIGN), auto close/reopen (3.3), amendment comment + body rewrite on addStory (3.2 AMENDMENT), three workflows retired with sync as a tool request (3.6, 3.7), adoption by recorded ref only (3.4), sub-issue links / task list / issue types / review comments kept and milestones dropped (2.4, 2.5, 3.1 item 9). No milestone code is added; ghEnsureMilestone/ghAttachMilestone are deleted.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The three push functions are declared at tracker-auto.ts:102, :165, :245 and their only production caller is the TUI approve service.","evidence":"src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts:102 `export function autoPushEpicOnHld`, :165 `autoPushStoryOnLld`, :245 `autoPushTasksOnPlan`. Grep over src finds non-test callers only at src/cli/services/workflow.ts:161-163 (`if (approval.workflow === 'design.epic') tracker = autoPushEpicOnHld(approval.path)` etc.); the rest are tracker-auto.test.ts and tracker-tasks.test.ts. The cited inner lines also match: label-pair adoption :122-123, label creation :129-131 and :289-291, title :133-134, pushedAt :148, comments :155-156 / :230-231 / :284, storyRefs spread :222, milestone calls :140 and :214. [files: src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"renderEpicBody never reads story refs today; only updateEpicTaskList writes the linked line; renderEpicBody's callers are autoPushEpicOnHld and the tracker.push context.","evidence":"conventions.ts:98 signature has four parameters; :114-117 pushes `- [ ] ${s.id}: ${s.title}${size}` for every story. updateEpicTaskList at :154-169 produces `- [ ] #${num} — ${storyId}: ${storyTitle}${suffix}`. Grep: renderEpicBody is called at tracker-auto.ts:138 and runners/tracker/context.ts:47, plus tracker.test.ts. updateEpicTaskList's only production caller is tracker-auto.ts:227. [files: src/workflow/tracker/conventions.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/tracker.test.ts]","action":"Minor: tracker.test.ts:21 imports updateEpicTaskList and :196-201 tests it. The design lists that file as a call site but does not say that test and import go; tsc does not compile tests, so say it in step 3 or the build will find it only by running the file.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The question-resolution comment is posted only from recordResolution's commitAndComment, gated on resolveGithubConfig alone, and only the resolve_question phase reaches it; the daemon's review-comment batch passes commit: false.","evidence":"questions.ts:383-393 recordResolution signature with `opts?: { readonly commit?: boolean }`; :424 `if (opts?.commit !== false)`; :460-480 commitAndComment, with :474-476 `const cfg = resolveGithubConfig(repoPath); if (cfg.type !== 'github') return; ghComment(...)`; trackerRef is epicRef at :317 and :329, storyRef at :340; resolvedAt stamped at :408. Grep `recordResolution(` outside tests: only src/mcp/workflow-step/phases/resolve-question.ts:78 (no opts passed). resolve-comment.ts:182 calls the seam with `{ commit: false }` and commits once in commitRecorded (:208-222); the seam type is at :44. Note: a second resolve of the same question re-stamps resolvedAt (:408), so it gets a new key and a new comment, as today; the 'posted once' guarantee only covers re-delivery of the same request. [files: src/workflow/questions.ts, src/mcp/workflow-step/phases/resolve-question.ts, src/workflow/resolve-comment.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"syncTracker is synchronous, gated on resolveGithubConfig plus ghAuthOk, reads with ghGetIssueState, and is reached only through the TUI service and the sync command.","evidence":"sync.ts:24 `export function syncTracker(repoPath: string, epicHash: string): SyncResult`; :36 resolveGithubConfig, :45 ghAuthOk, :49/:53 ghGetIssueState, :56 patches epicStatus/storyStatus/lastSyncedAt. Callers: src/cli/services/workflow.ts:308 `return syncTracker(repoPath, epicHash)`; services/index.ts:66 declares `sync(...): SyncResult`; command.ts:244 `const r = svc.workflow.sync(ctx.repoPath, rest[0])` inside `async function runWorkflow` (:164), so it can be awaited. No other `.sync(` caller in src/cli. [files: src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts, src/cli/command.ts, src/cli/services/index.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Everything this design says it reuses from the issues design (LLD-38436e90625a83a2-s1) is stated there with the shape used here.","evidence":"docs/standalone/add-add-items-tracker-setting-have-E2026100638436e90/S001/LLD.md line 134 defines linkUnder, itemType, the own asynchronous create returning ref and numeric id with untyped retry 'only on a definite refusal of the type', known-ref adoption ('The title is never changed'), `reopen(ref)`, `state(ref)` ('this design does not call it, and the companion design's sync request does'), sync listed as a request 'defined in the companion design', milestone helpers 'deleted by the companion design', and that addOrUpdate creates every passed label ('the companion design's kinds pass a third, epic:<slug>'). Line 149 defines the 5 minute budget, the comments map with the keys '<artifact id>:design:<approvedAt>', '<artifact id>:review:<reviewedAt>', the amendment id and '<artifact id>:question:<question id>:<resolvedAt>', taskClosedAt, patchTrackerMeta merged 'key by key' with a remove list, and the by-kind table extended by this design. Line 189 has `record: AmendmentRecord` and 'Rejecting an artifact and rejecting an amendment'. [files: docs/standalone/add-add-items-tracker-setting-have-E2026100638436e90/S001/LLD.md, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-38436e90625a83a2-s1.json]","action":"The issues design's JSON currently carries a passing daemon review (reviewedAt 2026-10-06T14:31:06Z) and no approvedAt. That matches section 3.1 and migration step 1, but the Summary ('the approved issues design') and reference c1 ('approved 2026-10-06') read as if it were approved now; reword on the next edit.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"What is called new does not exist yet: a retired-names list, and comments / closedAt / taskClosedAt on TrackerMeta with a key-by-key merge.","evidence":"Grep `RETIRED_WORKFLOW` in src: no match. refs.ts:24-37 TrackerMeta has no comments, closedAt, taskClosedAt or commentedOn field. refs.ts:94 is `{ adapter: 'github', ...prior, ...patch }`, a shallow merge with no way to remove a field, as both designs say. github.ts has no reopen helper (only ghCloseIssue at :199). [files: src/workflow/tracker/refs.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The three entry points that accept a workflow name are server.ts:472, server.ts:871 and workflow-rpc.ts:664, all driven by WORKFLOW_NAMES, so removing the names without a retired list makes the retired message unreachable.","evidence":"types.ts:73-87 declares WORKFLOW_NAMES with 'tracker.push'/'tracker.sync'/'tracker.post' at :82-84 and `WorkflowName = typeof WORKFLOW_NAMES[number]`. Grep WORKFLOW_NAMES: server.ts:472 and :871 `workflow: z.enum(WORKFLOW_NAMES)`, workflow-rpc.ts:664 `!(WORKFLOW_NAMES as readonly string[]).includes(workflow)` then throws `unknown workflow`. No other consumer except a brainstorm registration test. start.ts:121-127 is one condition over design.epic, design.story, plan, build and the three tracker names, taking `params['epicHash']` through assertEpicHash. [files: src/workflow/types.ts, src/mcp/server.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/mcp/workflow-step/phases/start.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The removal inventory for the three tracker workflows is complete in src.","evidence":"Grep `tracker\\.(push|sync|post)` over src returns exactly the files the design names: steering-block.md:297, start.ts:123, server.ts:420-422 and :458-460, synthesizer.ts:171-173, artifacts/tracker.ts, runners/tracker/index.ts and context.ts, chain.ts:298 and :306, orchestrator.ts:179-181, :297-299, :439-441 and the finalize from :2648 (mutateEpicTrackerMeta ends :2878), storage.ts:818, types.ts:82-84, and the tests tracker-e2e, tracker-tasks-coarse, tracker-artifact. Importers: artifacts/tracker.js only from orchestrator.ts:115 and its test; runners/tracker only from workflow/index.ts:19 (call at :34); linkDocsToIssues only from orchestrator.ts:130/:2856, so it can go. Outside src the names occur in the eight doc/site files the design lists and vscode-plugin/assets/steering-block.md. The guide's `tracker` key is carried by the markers at steering-block.md:296 and :304, so rewriting the section keeps insrc_guide and its tests working. [files: src/workflow/orchestrator.ts, src/workflow/index.ts, src/workflow/tracker/link.ts, src/prompts/steering-block.md]","action":"Four files under plans/ (workflow-implementation.md, workflow-design.md, workflow-define.md, review-cycle-and-streaming-completion.md) also name the workflows and are not mentioned; say they are history like the old approved designs, or add them to step 9.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The chain report's tracker next actions are at chain.ts:294-308 with kinds at :76-77 and formatter lines at :374-375, read from the Define at :206-215, and chain.test.ts asserts the old action.","evidence":"chain.ts:76-77 `'push-tracker'` / `'sync-tracker'`; :295-308 build commands `insrc_workflow_step phase=start workflow=tracker.push ...` and `workflow=tracker.sync ...`; :374-375 format them; :206-215 readTrackerMeta reads epicRef and lastSyncedAt off the Define. chain.test.ts:207-215 `assert.equal(r.nextAction.kind, 'push-tracker')`. [files: src/workflow/chain.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/chain.test.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.4","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ghEnsureMilestone, ghAttachMilestone and allTrackerLabels have no caller other than the three push functions, so they can be deleted with them while useMilestones stays on the config.","evidence":"Grep over src: ghEnsureMilestone (github.ts:225) and ghAttachMilestone (:233) are referenced only at tracker-auto.ts:40-41, :140, :214. allTrackerLabels (conventions.ts:49-50) only at tracker-auto.ts:45 and :129; no test references it. It returns `[epicLabel, storyLabel, epicMembershipLabel(epicSlug), ...STATUS_LABELS]` with STATUS_LABELS at :32, and setup.ts:85 is `SETUP_LABELS = ['insrc:epic', 'insrc:story', 'insrc:task', ...STATUS_LABELS]`. useMilestones is at config/github.ts:72, :110, :247, :275 and github.test.ts:145-168; its other readers are the tracker runners, which are deleted. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/conventions.ts, src/workflow/tracker/setup.ts, src/workflow/config/github.ts]","action":"After this design and the issues design, ghGetIssueState, ghFindIssueByLabels and ghCreateIssueTyped are left with no production caller; say whether they are deleted or kept.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"This repo has two epics with recorded refs, their Defines hold storyRefs, and a whole-body rewrite from the Define keeps the story links; 31 Defines exist and 29 were never tracked.","evidence":".insrc/artifacts/DEF-185807ba9a6b35d3.json meta.tracker: epicRef insors-ai/insrc#1, pushedAt, storyRefs s1..s5 -> #2..#6. DEF-6d6cfaf9a9b14bd4.json: epicRef insors-ai/insrc#41. Grep for \"epicRef\" across DEF/HLD files finds only these two hashes; Glob DEF-*.json returns 31 files. Story ids in the Define (s1..) match the keys used for BUILD records (for example BUILD-9b72686c1746af2b-s1.json), so the close rule can pair them. Neither tracked epic has a BUILD record, so the backfill adopts them and leaves both open. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-185807ba9a6b35d3.json, .insrc/artifacts/DEF-6d6cfaf9a9b14bd4.json]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Old records carry a ref and pushedAt but no comments map, so seeding the design and review keys at pushedAt stops the backfill repeating comments.","evidence":"tracker-auto.ts:148 patches `{ epicRef, pushedAt }` on the HLD, :219 `{ storyRef, pushedAt }` on the LLD, :314 `{ taskRefs, pushedAt }` on the plan; no comment key is recorded anywhere. The HLD, LLD and PLAN files of both tracked epics have pushedAt and no \"comments\" key. The rule is a safe approximation, not exact: the adopted paths write pushedAt without posting the design comment (:155 and :224 are inside `adopted === undefined`), and the tracker.push finalize writes `{ taskRefs, pushedAt }` on plans (orchestrator.ts:2863) without any review comment, so a few old records will be seeded for comments that were never posted. linkDocsToIssues (link.ts:49-52) writes refs without pushedAt, so those records are correctly not seeded. [files: src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts, src/workflow/tracker/link.ts]","action":"Add one sentence accepting that a seeded record may be missing a comment the old push skipped; the alternative, duplicating comments, is worse.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A story added by an extend joins the Define at extend time without clearing its approval and with a pending amendment, and every amendment type is an HLD change, so the design neither redesigns the extend path nor could have amended the standalone issues design.","evidence":"orchestrator.ts:1325 `const nextDefine = appendStoryToDefine(intent.repoPath, epicHash, story)` followed by an AmendmentRecord of type 'storyBoundary.addStory' with `status: 'pending'` (:1328-1344). gates.ts:175-186 appends to body.stories and rewrites the file with meta untouched ('PRESERVES meta.approvedAt'). amendments/types.ts declares eleven types (sharedContract.*, storyBoundary.*, nonFunctional.retarget, rollout.*), all HLD-level. approveAmendment is at store.ts:101 and stays unchanged; its TUI callers are services/workflow.ts:271-272, services/index.ts:63 and WorkflowsPane.tsx:119, as cited. The ownership split with the issues design is consistent on both sides (sync, the question comment and the milestone-helper deletion are assigned here by that design's own text). [files: src/workflow/orchestrator.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/amendments/types.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The failures the design handles are detectable where it says: a retired name today is rejected before any handler, sync with no epicRef answers skipped, and a comment failure after a resolution cannot fail the resolution.","evidence":"workflow-rpc.ts:664-665 throws `workflow.run: unknown workflow` for any name outside WORKFLOW_NAMES and server.ts:472/:871 validate with z.enum, which is why the retired list has to be accepted by the schema first. sync.ts:28-30 returns `{ status: 'skipped', reason: 'Epic not pushed yet (no epicRef in meta.tracker)' }` before any gh call (the wording differs from the design's 'the epic is not tracked'; behaviour is the same). resolve-question.ts is an async handler that awaits after recordResolution returns (:93), so it can await the new daemon request and log a failure; recordResolution has already written and committed by then (questions.ts:418-427). [files: src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts, src/mcp/workflow-step/phases/resolve-question.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac1-ac6 maps to named tests that are defined in the test levels, and the existing test files to be rewritten or deleted exist.","evidence":"Every id in the acceptance mapping (E1-E5, E7-E14, E16-E24, E26-E30) appears as a subject in section 5; E6, E15 and E25 are extra. The files named exist and exercise what the design says: tracker-auto.test.ts:24 and tracker-tasks.test.ts:26 import the three push functions; tracker-e2e.test.ts and tracker-tasks-coarse.test.ts drive 'tracker.push' through handleWorkflowStep; tracker-artifact.test.ts imports artifacts/tracker.js; chain.test.ts:215 asserts 'push-tracker'; schema-registry.test.ts exists. Stubs of the sync service in the CLI tests will need a Promise once the service type changes. [files: src/workflow/__tests__/tracker-auto.test.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/chain.test.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/tracker.test.ts]","action":"Name the removal of the updateEpicTaskList test (tracker.test.ts:196-201) and its import (:21) alongside E27, since that file is kept and edited rather than deleted.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":16,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-06T16:41:47.967Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
